id: pm-xa3t0o
title: Context calibration recovery names a nonexistent package script
description: "The mandatory context-intent calibration gate tells contributors to run pnpm context:intent:calibrate --update when the report drifts, but package.json declares no context:intent:calibrate script. The direct node command works, so the failure receipt points to an inexecutable recovery path precisely when a contributor needs it."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,context,quality-gate,recovery
created_at: "2026-08-16T12:30:22.924Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-16T12:35:13.633Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: The package manifest exposes the exact recovery command named by the calibration gate and it forwards update arguments correctly; A negative control removes or renames the script and proves gate recovery conformance fails; Testing documentation and the gate error use one executable spelling
parent: pm-mpbb
